<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4e16dfdfea236a0de5c9f6881e39513457402971" commit="1993805d06381fe5038548e2aad6cd5d20ab63f2" commit_message="anx7688: Add support for ANX7688  ANX7688 is a PD + HDMI-&gt;DP converter. It contains a firmware that we update from the AP-FW, at boot time, which is the only reason to have a driver for it in depthcharge.  We reuse the PD software sync mechanism, with some caveats as the chip does not have proper RO/RW sections.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52434 TEST=Boot elm-rev0  Change-Id: I4e16dfdfea236a0de5c9f6881e39513457402971 Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339497 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="339497" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="16" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/97/339497/16" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic6f3d19db03c740087e41638187349055bbe185c" commit="87967515222c0b019458b7993bcc17ffca5b30ea" commit_message="elm: Enable CONFIG_DRIVER_BUS_I2C_CROS_EC_TUNNEL  On elm board, we'd like to be able to talk to anx7688 through EC tunnel. We need the option enabled on oak as well, so that we can share the same firmware board file.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52442 TEST=Boot elm-rev0  Change-Id: Ic6f3d19db03c740087e41638187349055bbe185c Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350610 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="350610" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/10/350610/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibd7554d5b8ffb1c3416d939e4050c7b515ca0872" commit="f5ec8f9a943fd21f48584e937efceaf066619ffc" commit_message="elm: Enable CONFIG_DRIVER_EC_ANX7688  We also need the option on oak so that we can share the same board file.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52434 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ibd7554d5b8ffb1c3416d939e4050c7b515ca0872 Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339498 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="339498" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="15" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/98/339498/15" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4ecbdf5be5e501b70ccf679b4bd786bf5bfbdb39" commit="9e2812b605d332fe7c8116de2fedcb120e852ff1" commit_message="oak/elm: Add support for anx7688 as PD device.  Makes it possible to update ANX7688 FW from AP-FW.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52442 TEST=Boot elm-rev1  Change-Id: I4ecbdf5be5e501b70ccf679b4bd786bf5bfbdb39 Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339476 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="339476" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="17" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/76/339476/17" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Id78d375aca7a09839dfeb16d87f5e244cd4154b6" commit="6551ec918dac51562ba4df09b53ea2b0eac386f2" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: rockchip: Readjust how rk3399-kevin/gru do DVS voltages  Let's rejigger how rk3399-kevin and rk3399-gru handle DVS voltages. Specifically:  * Move the early operating point table for the CPU to its own dts   fragment so we don't have quite so many levels of inheritance.  For   now just include this fragment in the main gru dtsi file, but it will   eventually trickle to whichever revs had early silicon. * Switch to using 'regulator-microvolt-offset'.  We think that the early   bugs that we were hitting with this were all only related to   validating regulator constraints and with the PWM Regulator bugs fixed   these shouldn't be terribly important.  This allows us to get the   proper offset for _all_ DVS rails without tons of table overrides.  It   also is a slightly better description of what's happening.  The net-net is that when we turn on DVS for the GPU and or memory controller we should automatically get the adjustment needed for Kevin.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51368 TEST=Hack similar offset onto gru-gru and use servo to validate. TEST=See that centerlogic and gpu rails report BIOS set to 1.1V on gru      and 900mV on kevin, indicating that the offset is accounted for.  Change-Id: Id78d375aca7a09839dfeb16d87f5e244cd4154b6 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351040 Tested-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="351040" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/40/351040/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I17da056b1501b638cd703994f22763e55985422a" commit="15b3cc3464bbf82d3dae4f700ce954dff7e602df" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: rockchip: enable the gpu found on rk3399 gru  Enable the gpu and add the mali-supply power for rk3399 gru/kevin board.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51368 TEST=tested the gpu for kevin TEST=See /sys/class/devfreq/ff9a0000.gpu [2.482504] mali ff9a0000.gpu: GPU identified as 0x0860 r2p0 status 0 [2.508316] mali ff9a0000.gpu: Probed as mali0  Change-Id: I17da056b1501b638cd703994f22763e55985422a Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346377 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346377" owner_email="wxt@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="20" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/77/346377/20" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I3981deca42d8a0f2abe666531c510457a67cd1c1" commit="ca6573aeab3dd38d0d262209f6a410e0ead2d051" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: phy: ar8216: Improve the QM error WAR  When phy status change from down to up,it need set speed and duplex before enable auto-neg. The QM WAR need set LAN&amp;WAN port which forces mode when link down, so it will lead swconfig get wrong link status. Need to add more conditions check when get link status,if it's force mode but it's not the CPU port,then still net will get the status form related MAC status register.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52054 TEST=swconfig to show the port link status, should be correct when plugin the cable  or unplug the cable.  Change-Id: I3981deca42d8a0f2abe666531c510457a67cd1c1 Signed-off-by: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/347021 Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="347021" owner_email="ssambang@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/347021/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I12c95e2503aa20ae9baa77ff9a79cd6ed1c8602a" commit="93ac9ba2e5a5fdf5c9eb7f536c47d088e7dd4257" commit_message="cbuildbot: do not produce lakitu factory_install image  This change hard-codes the list of image types in lakitu base config, and excludes 'factory_install' type.  This has been done previously for the smaug board, which is also a part of _nofactory_boards.  TEST=Ran lakitu-release trybot. BUG=chromium:350163  Change-Id: I12c95e2503aa20ae9baa77ff9a79cd6ed1c8602a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350921 Commit-Ready: Amey Deshpande &lt;ameyd@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Amey Deshpande &lt;ameyd@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350921" owner_email="ameyd@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/21/350921/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Id058aeb962527982d607dc8f12b492c401dad4c4" commit="ed904ebf9df2f4a25f5dab84ae8b74492e740eac" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Handle invalid ilk pipe watermarks correctly.  This function returns an int, but when ilk_validate_pipe_wm fails it returns false, which is 0 (success). As a result invalid watermarks are applied, while they should have been rejected.  Fix this by returning -EINVAL.  Fixes: ed4a6a7ca853 (&quot;drm/i915: Add two-stage ILK-style watermark programming (v11)&quot;) Cc: Matt Roper &lt;matthew.d.roper@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Maarten Lankhorst &lt;maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1456918563-28696-1-git-send-email-maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com Reviewed-by: Matt Roper &lt;matthew.d.roper@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 1a426d6116467e09954289ee8c273e1bcc003adc from drm-intel-next-2016-03-14) Signed-off-by: Tarun Vyas &lt;tarun.vyas@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52640 TEST=Image builds, boots and is browse-able  Change-Id: Id058aeb962527982d607dc8f12b492c401dad4c4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344982 Commit-Ready: Tarun Vyas &lt;tarun.vyas@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344982" owner_email="tarun.vyas@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/344982/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2020c62426c2ccee7957b1a446a2f95e868f9c8d" commit="30787626e602e41cdf1cc6580c6b9c8a637dffdd" commit_message="autotest: Logcat support for testbeds.  Updates adb_host to append the device serial to the logcat filename. This will enable support for testbeds as each test has multiple devices.  BUG=b:29082270 TEST=./site_utils/test_droid.py -s ZX1G22KTSC,ZX1G22KMZ6 -r \ android1758-row1-rack7-test-station-5.cros testbed_DummyTest The resulting test results folder had 2 files: logcat_ZX1G22KTSC.log &amp; logcat_ZX1G22KMZ6.log  Change-Id: I2020c62426c2ccee7957b1a446a2f95e868f9c8d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350931 Commit-Ready: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350931" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/31/350931/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6be7fc3b7176728f85953ca840df3f48da8c749a" commit="ba8444a6c9b677869beac29f669ed9348953982e" commit_message="EC Unit Test: Improvements to mutex test  Fixed an issue with the simple contention test. The test intends to have task MTX2 grab the lock then have task MTX1 attempt to obtain the lock. However, task MTX2 would grab then release the lock prior task MTX1 trying to get the lock.  In addition, a new test was added to specfically test locking and release order. The test uses the existing random_task() function and verifies that all 3 tasks are pending on the lock being released. Following the lock release, the test also verifies that the pending task are run in highest to lowest priority order.  The issue description notes issues with the mass lock-unlocking test related to random time delays being used when run on the emmulator. Given that these tests are occasionally run on real target hardware, this test was not modified so that existing functionality was not modified.  BRANCH=none BUG=chromium:611086 TEST=Manual Ran 'make runtests' then ./build/host/mutex/mutex.exe to view console output. Verified that the tests pass and console log matched the expected output.  Change-Id: I6be7fc3b7176728f85953ca840df3f48da8c749a Signed-off-by: Scott &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344021 Commit-Ready: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="344021" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/21/344021/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibfdfb410902d3179743f8b31847fad9ef99cb08b" commit="de3cb7a0114200939f7613ffc4ab4b0aafcec0dd" commit_message="Revert &quot;chromeos_config: temporarily mark cheets paladins important=False&quot;  This reverts commit 10362aef0f02d42596748f6fef8a3776356d0d6c.  Change-Id: Ibfdfb410902d3179743f8b31847fad9ef99cb08b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351090 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="351090" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/90/351090/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie81bc6659312b0087e1cd0cd976603f68d5f13eb" commit="1c5e01e97dfd0eb042ad5e521166f219becccae7" commit_message="[autotest] Try to collect log files generated by act_cmd even if test failed.  BUG=b:29082270 TEST=run locally.  Change-Id: Ie81bc6659312b0087e1cd0cd976603f68d5f13eb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350898 Commit-Ready: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350898" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/98/350898/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8430.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>